ORACLE: the integer ranges of the sea value ops (InferIntRangeInterface,
lib/Dialect/Sea/SeaIntRanges.cpp) and the facts of sea-range-fold
(sea/Transforms/RangeFold.h) against the golden semantics (evalPureOp) at
widths 1-3 (casts and facts: up to 4): every value of every range tuple of
the generated set (all unsigned and signed intervals; their intersections:
all at widths 1-2, every 7th at width 3) is in the inferred range
(unittests/IntRanges). It catches, for example, upstream's x / 0 range (arith
UB) against sea's bvudiv x 0 = ~0.

RUN: sea-int-ranges-test | FileCheck %s
CHECK: failures: 0

